{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/shenko/pulls/384","id":5430468513,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVUFCKs8AAAABQ65foQ","html_url":"https://github.com/cyjin-yl/shenko/pull/384","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyjin-yl/shenko/pull/384.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyjin-yl/shenko/pull/384.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/shenko/issues/384","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/shenko/pulls/384/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/shenko/pulls/384/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/shenko/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/shenko/issues/384/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/shenko/statuses/5f1e426a047390159f038bf58b6d19948ab4ffc9","number":384,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix wait routing and Nightly setup; verify repeated real single-node journeys","user":{"login":"cyjin-yl","id":19223209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjIzMjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19223209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl","html_url":"https://github.com/cyjin-yl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Why\n\nA policy change could select a new model while the subject was still inside a semantic wait bound to its original model. The full Nightly suites also lacked the normal CI's native fixture setup, and the compiler browser suites ran in a root container that could not satisfy their sandbox contract. Existing real-journey evidence did not yet establish repeated completion and recovery on the authorized deployment.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Integrate #381 with its original history, and keep active semantic waits on the exact executable binding sealed at their origin. Expiry/end resumes ordinary routing; restart never renews the deadline.\n- Integrate #383 with its original history, preserving archive schema admission before payload or Store publication.\n- Share Node, DSH and native evidence setup between normal CI and Nightly. Run the complete pinned compiler suite as the hosted non-root user and verify Chromium's real sandbox.\n- Add opt-in, bounded, nonblocking Store phase timings and conservative timing summaries. These diagnostics do not change durable authority or represent physical-send receipts.\n- Extend the existing real browser/model/child/native journey with repeat accounting, fixed candidate/model observations, original-effect recovery comparisons and owned-process cleanup.\n\n## Validation in progress\n\n- The initial integration checkpoint `a716ff15` completed the full compiler Nightly: 183 suites passed, 2 skipped; 2,913 tests passed, 9 skipped. All ten previously blocked browser suites ran successfully with the real sandbox. [Run/job](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/shenko/actions/runs/44929495546/job/136922788338).\n- That Nightly's Rust suite exposed an existing synthetic semantic-wait fixture without an executable origin binding. Its fixture is being corrected without weakening runtime checks. The four earlier Node/artifact-directory failures and the explicit recovery/helper proofs passed.\n- [CI for `ecb0616c`](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/shenko/actions/runs/44930714203) and additional scoped checks are retained separately from the final candidate.\n- Real doescompute testing uses the observed `swift-qwen3.8-27b-nvfp4` deployment with checkpoint/template/config hashes. The first browser attempt stopped before inference because the witness still assumed append while the current one-send UI uses negotiated steer; the original failure is retained and the witness is being aligned with the actual public contract.\n\nThis remains draft until the final candidate's checks and bounded real journeys complete. It does not claim 7/30-day operation, full upgrade/rollback, multi-node acceptance, or that the deployed derived checkpoint is an untouched model reference.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-21T17:20:21Z","updated_at":"2026-11-21T21:41:56Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"3d6c1f436ba00082ba132a37217fca574cfa3bf0","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"cyjin-yl:feat/daily-readiness-20261122","ref":"feat/daily-readiness-20261122","repo":{"id":1430340138,"node_id":"R_kgDOVUFCKg","name":"shenko","full_name":"cyjin-yl/shenko","owner":{"login":"cyjin-yl","id":19223209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjIzMjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19223209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl","html_url":"https://github.com/cyjin-yl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/received_events","typ